  (text "Divider (W23, 2026-10-15): R304 220k / R305 10k, 0.1 % 25 ppm thin film, straight on VBAT_FUSED (after F101, ahead of D101), always on: about 0.1 mA at 24 V, 0.05 mA at 12 V\n(the battery feeds a CCTV camera continuously, owner Q8; no divider switch). Ratio 23.0: 0-69 V -> 0-3.0 V; one-point calibration in firmware (NVS).\nU301 ADS1115 at I2C 0x48: AIN0 = VBAT_TAP via R307 1k (PGA auto-range: 4.096 V FS -> 2.9 mV, 2.048 V -> 1.4 mV per LSB at the battery).\nALERT/RDY not connected: firmware polls the conversion (single-shot, OS bit of the config register).\nAIN1, AIN2, and AIN3 are unused (no-connect, allowed by SBAS444E 9.1.4; J502, R309, R310 removed per rework 2026-10-18).\nReversed alligator clips: the divider tap goes to about -1.4 V at -32 V; the 9.6k divider source plus R307 1k keep the ADS1115 AIN0 clamp current below 0.15 mA (10 mA limit).\nNo NTC and no current sense (owner Q4, Q6): future options only."
    (at 25.4 27.94 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "01009271-18e2-447f-943a-11bf5721a633")
  )
